{"title":"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>On each side of a unit square, an equilateral triangle of side length 1 is constructed. On each new side of each equilateral triangle, another equilateral triangle of side length 1 is constructed. The interiors of the square and the 12 triangles have no points in common. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the region formed by the union of the square and all the triangles, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the smallest convex polygon that contains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. What is the area of the region that is inside <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> but outside <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/c/03cda09c6f96b1ee9a102e90ec609d2c22ea1d26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)} \\; \\frac{1}{4} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)} \\; \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)} \\; 1 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)} \\; \\sqrt{3} \\qquad \\textbf{(E)} \\; 2 \\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"409\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7af6121e2831aa5bf8db7a271830fc340d0c5d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] real a = 1/2, b = sqrt(3)/2; draw((0,0)--(1,0)--(1,1)--(0,1)--cycle); draw((0,0)--(a,-b)--(1,0)--(1+b,a)--(1,1)--(a,1+b)--(0,1)--(-b,a)--(0,0)); draw((0,0)--(-1+a,-b)--(1+a,-b)--(1,0)--(1+b,-1+a)--(1+b,1+a)--(1,1)--(1+a,1+b)--(-1+a,1+b)--(0,1)--(-b,1+a)--(-b,-1+a)--(0,0)); filldraw((1+a,-b)--(1,0)--(1+b,-1+a)--cycle,gray(0.9)); filldraw((1+b,1+a)--(1,1)--(1+a,1+b)--cycle,gray(0.9)); filldraw((-1+a,1+b)--(0,1)--(-b,1+a)--cycle,gray(0.9)); filldraw((-b,-1+a)--(0,0)--(-1+a,-b)--cycle,gray(0.9)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p>The equilateral triangles form trapezoids with side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/4/bd4b4b96cedeaa282f935930ccb5928c5221496e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 1, 1, 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" /> (half a unit hexagon) on each face of the unit square.  The four triangles \"in between\" these trapezoids are isosceles triangles with two side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and an angle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73393067e6d6e401a5354accc7a730c7a2977aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> in between them, so the total area of these triangles (which is the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/e/21eefc2b9db61a1c8cacef6f069a0dadbfa1945f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S - R$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />) is, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/6/7368e0f6b590107c020e72c36894411a49164d7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\left( \\frac {1}{2} \\sin 30^{\\circ} \\right) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"138\" height=\"43\" /> which makes the answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/5/3f58d2efaaa17d28cec9dd927d78708a63b43e24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6ef509ed715cf1801d20e8dcbbaf70f0c4d7fe3c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] real a = 1/2, b = sqrt(3)/2; draw((0,0)--(1,0)--(1,1)--(0,1)--cycle); draw((a+b+a,a+b+a)--(a+b+a,-b)--(-b,-b)--(-b,a+a+b)--cycle,dashed); draw((0,0)--(a,-b)--(1,0)--(1+b,a)--(1,1)--(a,1+b)--(0,1)--(-b,a)--(0,0)); draw((0,0)--(-1+a,-b)--(1+a,-b)--(1,0)--(1+b,-1+a)--(1+b,1+a)--(1,1)--(1+a,1+b)--(-1+a,1+b)--(0,1)--(-b,1+a)--(-b,-1+a)--(0,0)); filldraw((1+a,-b)--(1,0)--(1+b,-1+a)--cycle,gray(0.9)); filldraw((1+b,1+a)--(1,1)--(1+a,1+b)--cycle,gray(0.9)); filldraw((-1+a,1+b)--(0,1)--(-b,1+a)--cycle,gray(0.9)); filldraw((-b,-1+a)--(0,0)--(-1+a,-b)--cycle,gray(0.9)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p>The area of the largest square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/0/eb05c099d6ddf2df70b23c1bd5db26a381304a8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1+\\sqrt{3})^2=4+2\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"168\" height=\"24\" />. The area of region <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/2/a62d325e29dcf5ebed3c517ccc2fa100e146bc2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+12\\frac{1}{2}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}=1+3\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"182\" height=\"43\" />. The total area of four small 45-45-90 triangles at corner is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/3/df3f97e1209ab0bbd1da4b3f67e76fe47b4aed21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4*\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}+1-2}{2})^2=2-\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"233\" height=\"43\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/2/e025613825fa50ddfb3f3fe6ef16650ec378d880.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S=4+2\\sqrt{3}-(2-\\sqrt{3})=2+3\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"284\" height=\"24\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/7/c478db9c690602b7e89dfa2971b7d8cf11e93a3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S-R=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n~Bran Qin\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?p=1051031#p1051031\">Region with Squares and Triangles</a>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B\">2008 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016224849\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nCo